@file Compfiles/CIIM2022P6.lean
@decl CIIM2022P6.sum_div_pow_le_one
-- L4DEL: title: Key combinatorial estimate
-- L4DEL: intuition: Key combinatorial estimate. Let `P` be a finset of primes with multiplicities `v p ≥ 1`, and set `N = ∏ p ∈ P, p ^ v p`. Then the sum of `(∏ p ∈ S, p ^ v p) / N ^ |S|` over nonempty `S ⊆ P` is at most `1`. (Proof: induction on `P`, peeling off one prime.) This is the exact estimate behind `d((n+1)!) ≤ 2 d(n!)`.
-- L4DEL: step: This explanation is a condensed rendering of the declaration's own doc comment at the pinned source commit; consult the exact Lean statement below for authority.

