@file Compfiles/Imo1986P6.lean
@decl Imo1986P6.imo1986_p6
-- L4DEL: title: Documented declaration: imo1986_p6
-- L4DEL: intuition: **IMO 1986, Problem 6.** Given a finite set `S` of points in the plane with integer coordinates, the points can be colored red or white so that on every line parallel to one of the coordinate axes the numbers of white and red points differ by at most one. We encode the coloring by a sign function `ε : ℤ × ℤ → ℤ` with values in `{1, -1}` (`1` = white, `-1` = red); the sum of `ε` over the points of `S` on a line is then exactly the difference between the numbers of white and red points on that line.
-- L4DEL: step: This explanation is a condensed rendering of the declaration's own doc comment at the pinned source commit; consult the exact Lean statement below for authority.

@file Compfiles/Imo1986P6.lean
@decl Imo1986P6.main_lemma
