-- L4DEL: intuition: Main induction: every finite set of points with integer coordinates admits a balanced signing.
-- L4DEL: step: This explanation is a condensed rendering of the declaration's own doc comment at the pinned source commit; consult the exact Lean statement below for authority.

@file Compfiles/Imo1986P6.lean
@decl Imo1986P6.pair_sum_zero
-- L4DEL: title: Documented declaration: pair_sum_zero
-- L4DEL: intuition: If a list of points with no repetitions has even length and a sign function alternates on each pair of consecutive elements while a "coordinate" function is constant on each pair, then the sum of the signs over the points of the list lying on any fixed level of the coordinate is zero. This is the computation showing that a correctly colored cycle contributes equally many white and red points to every row and every column.
-- L4DEL: step: This explanation is a condensed rendering of the declaration's own doc comment at the pinned source commit; consult the exact Lean statement below for authority.

