@file Compfiles/Imo1987P1.lean
@decl Imo1987P1.fixedPointsEquiv'
-- L4DEL: title: The set of triples `(k ≤ card α, σ ∈ fiber α k, x ∈ fixedPoints σ)` is equivalent to the set of pairs `(x : α, σ : Perm α)` such that `σ x = x`
-- L4DEL: intuition: The set of triples `(k ≤ card α, σ ∈ fiber α k, x ∈ fixedPoints σ)` is equivalent to the set of pairs `(x : α, σ : Perm α)` such that `σ x = x`. The equivalence sends `(k, σ, x)` to `(x, σ)` and `(x, σ)` to `(card (fixedPoints σ), σ, x)`. It is easy to see that the cardinality of the LHS is given by `∑ k : Fin (card α + 1), k * p α k`.
-- L4DEL: step: This explanation is a condensed rendering of the declaration's own doc comment at the pinned source commit; consult the exact Lean statement below for authority.

