@file Compfiles/Imo2000P3.lean
@decl Imo2000P3.AllRightOf
-- L4DEL: title: Documented declaration: AllRightOf
-- L4DEL: intuition: The property of `lam` in the problem: starting from any initial configuration in which the fleas are not all at the same point, for every point `M` on the line there is a finite sequence of moves taking all the fleas strictly to the right of `M`.
-- L4DEL: step: This explanation is a condensed rendering of the declaration's own doc comment at the pinned source commit; consult the exact Lean statement below for authority.

@file Compfiles/Imo2000P3.lean
@decl Imo2000P3.allRightOf_of_ge
-- L4DEL: title: Documented declaration: allRightOf_of_ge
-- L4DEL: intuition: Sufficiency: if `1 / (n - 1) ≤ lam`, then Woeginger's strategy (first move the rightmost flea far enough to the right by repeatedly jumping the leftmost flea over it, then jump every other flea over the rightmost flea) takes all fleas to the right of any given point `M`.
-- L4DEL: step: This explanation is a condensed rendering of the declaration's own doc comment at the pinned source commit; consult the exact Lean statement below for authority.

@file Compfiles/Imo2000P3.lean
@decl Imo2000P3.leftmost
-- L4DEL: title: The position of the leftmost flea
-- L4DEL: intuition: The position of the leftmost flea.
-- L4DEL: step: This explanation is a condensed rendering of the declaration's own doc comment at the pinned source commit; consult the exact Lean statement below for authority.

@file Compfiles/Imo2000P3.lean
@decl Imo2000P3.Move
-- L4DEL: title: Documented declaration: Move
-- L4DEL: intuition: A single move with jump ratio `lam`: flea `i`, sitting at some point `A = x i`, jumps over flea `j` at `B = x j` (with `A` to the left of `B`) and lands at the point `C = B + lam * (B - A)`, so that `BC / AB = lam`. All other fleas stay put.
-- L4DEL: step: This explanation is a condensed rendering of the declaration's own doc comment at the pinned source commit; consult the exact Lean statement below for authority.

@file Compfiles/Imo2000P3.lean
@decl Imo2000P3.move_potential_bound
-- L4DEL: title: The key inequality for the necessity direction: a single move decreases the potential by at least `(1 / lam - (n - 1))` times the amount by which the rightmost flea advances
-- L4DEL: intuition: The key inequality for the necessity direction: a single move decreases the potential by at least `(1 / lam - (n - 1))` times the amount by which the rightmost flea advances.
-- L4DEL: step: This explanation is a condensed rendering of the declaration's own doc comment at the pinned source commit; consult the exact Lean statement below for authority.

@file Compfiles/Imo2000P3.lean
@decl Imo2000P3.not_allRightOf_of_lt
-- L4DEL: title: Necessity: if `0 < lam < 1 / (n - 1)`, then the rightmost flea stays bounded, so the fleas cannot all be moved arbitrarily far to the right
-- L4DEL: intuition: Necessity: if `0 < lam < 1 / (n - 1)`, then the rightmost flea stays bounded, so the fleas cannot all be moved arbitrarily far to the right.
-- L4DEL: step: This explanation is a condensed rendering of the declaration's own doc comment at the pinned source commit; consult the exact Lean statement below for authority.

@file Compfiles/Imo2000P3.lean
@decl Imo2000P3.phase1
-- L4DEL: title: Phase 1 of the strategy: after `t` moves of `strat_step`, the rightmost flea has advanced by at least `t` times the fixed positive amount `lam * potential x / (n - 1)`
-- L4DEL: intuition: Phase 1 of the strategy: after `t` moves of `strat_step`, the rightmost flea has advanced by at least `t` times the fixed positive amount `lam * potential x / (n - 1)`.
-- L4DEL: step: This explanation is a condensed rendering of the declaration's own doc comment at the pinned source commit; consult the exact Lean statement below for authority.

@file Compfiles/Imo2000P3.lean
@decl Imo2000P3.phase2
-- L4DEL: title: Documented declaration: phase2
-- L4DEL: intuition: Phase 2 of the strategy: if the rightmost flea is already to the right of `M`, then one can move every remaining flea to the right of `M`, one at a time, by jumping it over the rightmost flea.
-- L4DEL: step: This explanation is a condensed rendering of the declaration's own doc comment at the pinned source commit; consult the exact Lean statement below for authority.

