@file Compfiles/Imo2005P6.lean
@decl Imo2005P6.pairCount_modEq
-- L4DEL: title: Documented declaration: pairCount_modEq
-- L4DEL: intuition: The congruences: for every pair `P ⊆ {0, 1, 2, 3, 4}` of problems, writing `T` for the complementary triple, the number of contestants solving `P` is congruent modulo `3` to `1 + ∑_{u ∈ T} (contestants solving {u, 5}) + ∑_{Q ∈ T choose 2} (contestants solving Q)`. This holds per contestant: the distinguished contestant `c0` (who solved exactly `{0, 1, 2, 3, 4}`) contributes `-2 ≡ 1`, and every other contestant, who solved exactly four problems, contributes a multiple of `3` (see `cong_aux`).
-- L4DEL: step: This explanation is a condensed rendering of the declaration's own doc comment at the pinned source commit; consult the exact Lean statement below for authority.

