@file Compfiles/Imo2011P4.lean
@decl Imo2011P4.validSeq_insert
-- L4DEL: title: Documented declaration: validSeq_insert
-- L4DEL: intuition: Inserting the weight `2^0` into a valid sequence of doubled weights preserves validity: prefixes before the insertion point keep their (nonnegative, doubled) imbalance; later prefixes have imbalance `2d ± 1` with `d ≥ 0`, and when the new weight goes on the right pan the insertion is not at the beginning, so `d ≠ 0` (a nonempty signed sum of distinct powers of two), hence `d ≥ 1`.
-- L4DEL: step: This explanation is a condensed rendering of the declaration's own doc comment at the pinned source commit; consult the exact Lean statement below for authority.

@file Compfiles/Imo2011P4.lean
@decl Imo2011P4.validSeq_remove
-- L4DEL: title: Documented declaration: validSeq_remove
-- L4DEL: intuition: Removing the weight `2^0` and halving preserves validity: before the removed weight the imbalances are unchanged, and afterwards the (even) imbalance without the `±1` contribution can only drop by `1`, so it stays nonnegative.
-- L4DEL: step: This explanation is a condensed rendering of the declaration's own doc comment at the pinned source commit; consult the exact Lean statement below for authority.

