@file Compfiles/Imo2014P2.lean
@decl Imo2014P2.covering_restrict
-- L4DEL: title: Restriction reduction: a rook-covering configuration on an `M × M` board restricts (top-left, then completed arbitrarily) to one on any smaller `N × N` board
-- L4DEL: intuition: Restriction reduction: a rook-covering configuration on an `M × M` board restricts (top-left, then completed arbitrarily) to one on any smaller `N × N` board. The key point: every `K × K` square of the `N × N` board lies inside `[0,N)²`, so its witnessing rook already has both coordinates `< N` and survives the restriction; the arbitrary completion only adds rooks.
-- L4DEL: step: This explanation is a condensed rendering of the declaration's own doc comment at the pinned source commit; consult the exact Lean statement below for authority.

@file Compfiles/Imo2014P2.lean
@decl Imo2014P2.exists_config_no_square
-- L4DEL: title: Optimality (upper bound): some peaceful configuration has no empty `(⌊√(n-1)⌋+1) × (⌊√(n-1)⌋+1)` square
-- L4DEL: intuition: Optimality (upper bound): some peaceful configuration has no empty `(⌊√(n-1)⌋+1) × (⌊√(n-1)⌋+1)` square.
-- L4DEL: step: This explanation is a condensed rendering of the declaration's own doc comment at the pinned source commit; consult the exact Lean statement below for authority.

@file Compfiles/Imo2014P2.lean
@decl Imo2014P2.exists_empty_square
-- L4DEL: title: Existence (lower bound): every peaceful configuration has an empty `⌊√(n-1)⌋ × ⌊√(n-1)⌋` square
-- L4DEL: intuition: Existence (lower bound): every peaceful configuration has an empty `⌊√(n-1)⌋ × ⌊√(n-1)⌋` square. Following Evan Chen: let `R` be the rook in the top row, in column `col₀`, and stack `k` squares of size `k × k` directly below it. The `k` columns of that stack contain `k` rooks in total, but `R`'s rook sits at row `0`, above the stack — so the stack holds at most `k - 1` rooks among `k` disjoint squares, and one of them is empty.
-- L4DEL: step: This explanation is a condensed rendering of the declaration's own doc comment at the pinned source commit; consult the exact Lean statement below for authority.

@file Compfiles/Imo2014P2.lean
@decl Imo2014P2.HasEmptySquare
-- L4DEL: title: A peaceful configuration of `n` rooks is a permutation `σ`: the rook in row `i` sits in column `σ i`
-- L4DEL: intuition: A peaceful configuration of `n` rooks is a permutation `σ`: the rook in row `i` sits in column `σ i`. Such a configuration has a rook-free `k × k` square if there is a block of `k` consecutive rows and `k` consecutive columns (fitting on the board) containing no rook.
-- L4DEL: step: This explanation is a condensed rendering of the declaration's own doc comment at the pinned source commit; consult the exact Lean statement below for authority.

@file Compfiles/Imo2014P2.lean
@decl Imo2014P2.hasEmptySquare_mono
-- L4DEL: title: An empty `k × k` square contains an empty `j × j` square whenever `j ≤ k`
-- L4DEL: intuition: An empty `k × k` square contains an empty `j × j` square whenever `j ≤ k`.
-- L4DEL: step: This explanation is a condensed rendering of the declaration's own doc comment at the pinned source commit; consult the exact Lean statement below for authority.

