@file Compfiles/Imo2018P5.lean
@decl Imo2018P5.step
-- L4DEL: title: The key per-step relation
-- L4DEL: intuition: The key per-step relation. If `S n` and `S (n+1)` are both integers, then there is an integer `k` (namely `a₀·aₙ₋₁/aₙ`) with `aₙ * k = a₀ * aₙ₋₁` and `a₀ ∣ k + aₙ - aₙ₋₁`.
-- L4DEL: step: This explanation is a condensed rendering of the declaration's own leading source comment at the pinned source commit; consult the exact Lean statement below for authority.

@file Compfiles/Imo2018P5.lean
@decl Imo2018P5.val_rule
-- L4DEL: title: The valuation rule
-- L4DEL: intuition: The valuation rule. For a prime `p`, write `α, κ, V, V'` for the `p`-adic valuations of `a₀, k, aₙ₋₁, aₙ` respectively, where `k` comes from `step`. Then: `κ < α` forces `V = κ` and `V' = α`; `κ = α` forces `V' = V`; `α < κ` forces `α ≤ V' < V`.
-- L4DEL: step: This explanation is a condensed rendering of the declaration's own leading source comment at the pinned source commit; consult the exact Lean statement below for authority.

@file Compfiles/Imo2018P5.lean
@decl Imo2018P5.walk_const
-- L4DEL: title: No closed walk
-- L4DEL: intuition: No closed walk. If the sequence returns to the same value (`a n₁ = a n₂` with `n₁ < n₂`, `N ≤ n₁`), then it was constant on the whole interval `[n₁, n₂]`.
-- L4DEL: step: This explanation is a condensed rendering of the declaration's own leading source comment at the pinned source commit; consult the exact Lean statement below for authority.

