@file Compfiles/Imo2026P4.lean
@decl Imo2026P4.MulanWins
-- L4DEL: title: The set of triangles from which Mulan can force, in finitely many steps, a triangle with an interior angle equal to `θ`, no matter how Shan-Yu discards
-- L4DEL: intuition: The set of triangles from which Mulan can force, in finitely many steps, a triangle with an interior angle equal to `θ`, no matter how Shan-Yu discards. This is the least predicate closed under: * (`win`) if the current triangle already has an angle equal to `θ`, Mulan has won; * (`move`) if Mulan can make a cut producing children `L` and `R` from *both* of which she wins (so whichever one Shan-Yu keeps, she still wins), then she wins from the current triangle. Membership means Mulan wins in finitely many steps.
-- L4DEL: step: This explanation is a condensed rendering of the declaration's own doc comment at the pinned source commit; consult the exact Lean statement below for authority.

