@file Compfiles/Usa1974P4.lean
@decl Usa1974P4.probWinA
-- L4DEL: title: Documented declaration: probWinA
-- L4DEL: intuition: The probability that player `A` wins the series, where * `win x y` is the probability that `x` beats `y` in a single game, * the next game is played between `w` (the winner of the previous game) and `i` (the player who sat out the previous game); the loser of a game sits out the next one, * `hist` is the list of winners of the games played so far, and * `n` is a fuel bounding the number of games still to be played. The series ends as soon as some player has won two games in total, so it lasts at most four games: if no one has won twice after three games then the three winners so far are three distinct players, and the fourth game is played between two of them, so its winner reaches two wins.
-- L4DEL: step: This explanation is a condensed rendering of the declaration's own doc comment at the pinned source commit; consult the exact Lean statement below for authority.

