@file Compfiles/Usa1977P3.lean
@decl Usa1977P3.sextic_of_zero_remainder
-- L4DEL: title: Suppose that `x ^ 4 + x ^ 3 - 1` is divisible by the quadratic `x ^ 2 - s * x + p`, i.e
-- L4DEL: intuition: Suppose that `x ^ 4 + x ^ 3 - 1` is divisible by the quadratic `x ^ 2 - s * x + p`, i.e. both coefficients of the remainder `(s ^ 3 + s ^ 2 - 2 * p * s - p) * x + (p ^ 2 - p * (s ^ 2 + s) - 1)` of the long division vanish. Then `p` is a root of the sextic `x ^ 6 + x ^ 4 + x ^ 3 - x ^ 2 - 1`. This is the Vieta elimination step of the problem: writing the four roots of the quartic as `a, b, c, d` with `s = a + b` and `p = a * b`, the two remainder relations are exactly the third and fourth elementary symmetric relations between the roots.
-- L4DEL: step: This explanation is a condensed rendering of the declaration's own doc comment at the pinned source commit; consult the exact Lean statement below for authority.

@file Compfiles/Usa1977P5.lean
@decl Usa1977P5.cornerMax
-- L4DEL: title: Documented declaration: cornerMax
-- L4DEL: intuition: `cornerMax h k r s n` is the maximum, over all ways of choosing each of `n` further variables to be either `h` or `k`, of `(r + sum of the choices) * (s + sum of the reciprocals of the choices)`. It is defined recursively; the leaves of the recursion are exactly the `2 ^ n` "corner" values.
-- L4DEL: step: This explanation is a condensed rendering of the declaration's own doc comment at the pinned source commit; consult the exact Lean statement below for authority.

@file Compfiles/Usa1977P5.lean
@decl Usa1977P5.le_cornerMax
-- L4DEL: title: The product `(r + Σ f i) * (s + Σ 1 / f i)`, where each `f i ∈ [h, k]`, is bounded above by the corresponding corner maximum
-- L4DEL: intuition: The product `(r + Σ f i) * (s + Σ 1 / f i)`, where each `f i ∈ [h, k]`, is bounded above by the corresponding corner maximum. Proved by induction on `n`, applying `le_max_endpoint` to one variable at a time.
-- L4DEL: step: This explanation is a condensed rendering of the declaration's own doc comment at the pinned source commit; consult the exact Lean statement below for authority.

@file Compfiles/Usa1977P5.lean
@decl Usa1977P5.le_max_endpoint
-- L4DEL: title: Documented declaration: le_max_endpoint
-- L4DEL: intuition: If `r ≥ 0` and `0 < a ≤ x ≤ b`, then `(r + x) * (s + 1 / x)` is bounded above by the maximum of its values at the endpoints `x = a` and `x = b` (as a function of `x` it is a sum of `rs + 1`, the linear function `s * x` and the convex function `r / x`, hence it attains its maximum on `[a, b]` at an endpoint).
-- L4DEL: step: This explanation is a condensed rendering of the declaration's own doc comment at the pinned source commit; consult the exact Lean statement below for authority.

