@file Compfiles/Usa1986P1.lean
@decl Usa1986P1.eq_of_dvd
-- L4DEL: title: Documented declaration: eq_of_dvd
-- L4DEL: intuition: If the same prime `p ∈ {7, 11}` divides both `a + 2 * j₁` and `a + 2 * j₂` with `j₁, j₂ < 7`, then `j₁ = j₂`: `p` divides `2 * (j₂ - j₁)`, which has absolute value less than `14`, so it must be zero.
-- L4DEL: step: This explanation is a condensed rendering of the declaration's own doc comment at the pinned source commit; consult the exact Lean statement below for authority.

@file Compfiles/Usa1986P1.lean
@decl Usa1986P1.not_all_divisible
-- L4DEL: title: Among any seven consecutive odd numbers `a, a + 2, …, a + 12`, at least one is divisible by none of the primes `3, 5, 7, 11`
-- L4DEL: intuition: Among any seven consecutive odd numbers `a, a + 2, …, a + 12`, at least one is divisible by none of the primes `3, 5, 7, 11`. The proof follows the classical USAMO solution. At most three of the seven numbers are divisible by `3` (and if there are three, the two endpoints are among them), at most two by `5` (and then an endpoint is among them), at most one by `7` and at most one by `11`, so at most six of the seven numbers can be divisible by one of `3, 5, 7, 11`. We check the finitely many cases for `a % 3` and `a % 5`: in each case three explicit indices avoid `3` and `5`, and `not_all_divisible_of_three` finishes.
-- L4DEL: step: This explanation is a condensed rendering of the declaration's own doc comment at the pinned source commit; consult the exact Lean statement below for authority.

@file Compfiles/Usa1986P1.lean
@decl Usa1986P1.not_all_divisible_of_three
-- L4DEL: title: Documented declaration: not_all_divisible_of_three
-- L4DEL: intuition: Pigeonhole principle: among three pairwise distinct indices `t₁, t₂, t₃ < 7`, it cannot happen that each of `a + 2 * t₁`, `a + 2 * t₂`, `a + 2 * t₃` is divisible by `7` or by `11` (two of them would share a prime, contradicting `eq_of_dvd`). Hence, if none of them is divisible by `3` or `5`, one of them is divisible by none of `3, 5, 7, 11`.
-- L4DEL: step: This explanation is a condensed rendering of the declaration's own doc comment at the pinned source commit; consult the exact Lean statement below for authority.

@file Compfiles/Usa1986P1.lean
