@file Compfiles/Usa1992P3.lean
@decl Usa1992P3.gap
-- L4DEL: title: The key gap lemma: writing `s j` for the sum of the `j` smallest elements, if `s j < 1500` then the next element satisfies `a j ≤ s j + 1`
-- L4DEL: intuition: The key gap lemma: writing `s j` for the sum of the `j` smallest elements, if `s j < 1500` then the next element satisfies `a j ≤ s j + 1`. Indeed, `s j + 1 ≤ 1500` must occur as a subset sum, and any subset with that sum must contain some `a i` with `i ≥ j`, so `a j ≤ a i ≤ s j + 1`.
-- L4DEL: step: This explanation is a condensed rendering of the declaration's own doc comment at the pinned source commit; consult the exact Lean statement below for authority.

