-- L4DEL: intuition: A case analysis on `ZMod 3`: the key local identity behind the invariance of `totalWeight`. If `x` differs from both `L` and `R` and `v` differs from all of `x`, `L` and `R`, then the two pairs through `x` and through `v` have the same total weight. (This forces `L = R`, and each side of the identity vanishes.)
