@file Compfiles/Usa1995P1.lean
@decl Usa1995P1.exists_mem_digits_pred
-- L4DEL: title: The non-existence part: among the values `bSeq p i` there is no arithmetic progression of length `p`
-- L4DEL: intuition: The non-existence part: among the values `bSeq p i` there is no arithmetic progression of length `p`. If `x, x + d, …, x + (p-1) d` are all digit-free and `d > 0`, then looking at the least significant nonzero base-`p` digit of `d`, the `k`-th digits of the progression terms run through all residues mod `p`, so one of them equals `p - 1`: contradiction.
-- L4DEL: step: This explanation is a condensed rendering of the declaration's own doc comment at the pinned source commit; consult the exact Lean statement below for authority.

@file Compfiles/Usa1995P1.lean
@decl Usa1995P1.HasAp
-- L4DEL: title: Documented declaration: HasAp
-- L4DEL: intuition: `HasAp a p n m` means that the first `n + 1` terms `a 0, a 1, …, a (n-1), m` (where the candidate `m` is the `n`-th term) contain an arithmetic progression of length `p`: there are strictly increasing indices `v 0 < v 1 < … < v (p-1)`, all at most `n`, whose values form an arithmetic progression. The last conjunct splits the value condition according to whether the index is the final position `n` (where the candidate `m` sits) or not.
-- L4DEL: step: This explanation is a condensed rendering of the declaration's own doc comment at the pinned source commit; consult the exact Lean statement below for authority.

