@decl Usa1995P1.hasAp_of_mem_digits_pred
-- L4DEL: title: Documented declaration: hasAp_of_mem_digits_pred
-- L4DEL: intuition: The construction part: if `m < bSeq p n` has a base-`p` digit equal to `p - 1`, then reducing every such digit of `m` by `j` (for `j = p-1, …, 0`) gives an arithmetic progression of length `p` whose first `p - 1` terms are digit-free, hence equal to `a` at indices below `n`.
-- L4DEL: step: This explanation is a condensed rendering of the declaration's own doc comment at the pinned source commit; consult the exact Lean statement below for authority.

