@file Compfiles/Usa1997P3.lean
@decl Usa1997P3.good_unique
-- L4DEL: title: Uniqueness: the difference `D` of two good polynomials has coefficients in `{-9, …, 9}` and vanishes at `-2` and `-5`
-- L4DEL: intuition: Uniqueness: the difference `D` of two good polynomials has coefficients in `{-9, …, 9}` and vanishes at `-2` and `-5`. Its trailing coefficient is then divisible by both 2 and 5, hence by 10, hence it is zero — a contradiction unless `D = 0`.
-- L4DEL: step: This explanation is a condensed rendering of the declaration's own doc comment at the pinned source commit; consult the exact Lean statement below for authority.

