-- L4DEL: title: Documented declaration: card_construction
-- L4DEL: intuition: The `constructorNameAsVariable` linter normalizes the types of all binders; here those are memberships in concrete finsets on the `1000 × 1000` board, whose `whnf` unfolds a 1000-element list and exceeds the recursion limit.
-- L4DEL: step: This explanation is a condensed rendering of the declaration's own leading source comment at the pinned source commit; consult the exact Lean statement below for authority.

@file Compfiles/Usa2000P4.lean
@decl Usa2000P4.card_le_of_good
-- L4DEL: title: Upper bound: a good set on an `m × n` board with `m, n ≥ 2` has at most `m + n - 2` squares
-- L4DEL: intuition: Upper bound: a good set on an `m × n` board with `m, n ≥ 2` has at most `m + n - 2` squares. Proof: call a row (resp. column) *light* if it contains exactly one chosen square and *heavy* if it contains at least two. The squares lying in light rows are in bijection with the light rows, and every square in a heavy row is the unique chosen square of its column (by `alone_of_good`), so the squares in heavy rows inject into the light columns. Hence `|S| ≤ (#light rows) + (#light columns)`. If there is at least one heavy row and one heavy column, this is at most `m + n - 2`; if there is no heavy row then `|S| ≤ m`, and if there is no heavy column then `|S| ≤ n`.
-- L4DEL: step: This explanation is a condensed rendering of the declaration's own doc comment at the pinned source commit; consult the exact Lean statement below for authority.

