-- L4DEL: intuition: Let `p` be a nonzero real polynomial of degree `n` whose values at the integers `1, ..., n` alternate in sign, so that `p` has a root in each of the `n - 1` intervals `(i, i+1)`. If moreover `p` changes sign on one of the two "tails" `(-∞, 1)` or `(n, ∞)`, then `p` has exactly `n` real roots and splits.
