-- L4DEL: intuition: The pairing of the cells of the first two rows: the cell `(0, j)` is paired with `(1, colMate j)` and vice versa; all other cells are paired with themselves. Paired cells are in different rows and three columns apart, so they do not even share a vertex.
-- L4DEL: step: This explanation is a condensed rendering of the declaration's own doc comment at the pinned source commit; consult the exact Lean statement below for authority.

@file Compfiles/Usa2004P4.lean
@decl Usa2004P4.not_aliceWins
-- L4DEL: title: Documented declaration: not_aliceWins
-- L4DEL: intuition: The key endgame lemma: if the black cell of row 1 is the mate of the black cell of row 0, then the two black cells are three columns apart, so no black chain can leave row 0, and Alice cannot win.
-- L4DEL: step: This explanation is a condensed rendering of the declaration's own doc comment at the pinned source commit; consult the exact Lean statement below for authority.

