@decl Usa2007P3.color_eq
-- L4DEL: title: If every `(n+1)`-element subset `U` of `S` is monochromatic (i.e
-- L4DEL: intuition: If every `(n+1)`-element subset `U` of `S` is monochromatic (i.e. all of its `n`-element subsets have the same color), then all `n`-element subsets of `S` have the same color: any two `n`-element sets can be joined by a chain in which consecutive sets differ in exactly one element, so induction on the size of the symmetric difference applies.
-- L4DEL: step: This explanation is a condensed rendering of the declaration's own doc comment at the pinned source commit; consult the exact Lean statement below for authority.

