-- L4DEL: intuition: Unfolding lemma for `cross`. Do not use `simp only [cross]` or `cross.eq_unfold`: re-elaborating the auto-generated equation lemma hits the recursion depth limit.
-- L4DEL: step: This explanation is a condensed rendering of the declaration's own doc comment at the pinned source commit; consult the exact Lean statement below for authority.

@file Compfiles/Usa2007P4.lean
@decl Usa2007P4.crossAux
-- L4DEL: title: The body of `cross`, kept reducible so that membership and cardinality can be unfolded in the auxiliary lemmas `mem_aux` and `card_aux`
-- L4DEL: intuition: The body of `cross`, kept reducible so that membership and cardinality can be unfolded in the auxiliary lemmas `mem_aux` and `card_aux`. (In this environment, `Finset.Icc` on `ℤ` records a `Preorder ℤ` instance whose term contains the noncomputable `Int.instConditionallyCompleteLinearOrder`, hence the `noncomputable` keyword.)
