@decl Usa2008P5.move_lemma
-- L4DEL: title: One step of the first phase of the strategy: if `r k ≤ r i`, we may erase `r i` writing `r i - r k`, and update the coefficients accordingly
-- L4DEL: intuition: One step of the first phase of the strategy: if `r k ≤ r i`, we may erase `r i` writing `r i - r k`, and update the coefficients accordingly. The new coefficients still give a zero-sum relation, are not all zero, and their weight strictly decreases, provided that `(a k + a i).natAbs < (a k).natAbs`.
-- L4DEL: step: This explanation is a condensed rendering of the declaration's own doc comment at the pinned source commit; consult the exact Lean statement below for authority.

