@file Compfiles/Usa2010P2.lean
@decl Usa2010P2.alternation
-- L4DEL: title: The key alternation lemma
-- L4DEL: intuition: The key alternation lemma. Along any legal sequence of switches, the switches of the pair `(a, b)` and those of the pair `(a+1, b)` alternate, and every switch of `(a, b)` after the first one is preceded by a switch of `(a+1, b)`. Consequently the two displayed inequalities hold (the first conjunct applies when the initial cyclic-order state is A, the second when it is not).
-- L4DEL: step: This explanation is a condensed rendering of the declaration's own doc comment at the pinned source commit; consult the exact Lean statement below for authority.

