@file Compfiles/Usa2010P2.lean
@decl Usa2010P2.usa2010_p2
-- L4DEL: title: USAMO 2010 Problem 2.** There are `n` students standing in a circle, one behind the other, with heights `h₁ < h₂ < ⋯ < hₙ`
-- L4DEL: intuition: **USAMO 2010 Problem 2.** There are `n` students standing in a circle, one behind the other, with heights `h₁ < h₂ < ⋯ < hₙ`. If a student with height `hₖ` is standing directly behind a student with height `hₖ₋₂` or less, the two students are permitted to switch places. Then it is not possible to make more than `C(n, 3)` such switches. We model the circle by positions in `ZMod n` (position `p + 1` is directly behind position `p`), the students by their height ranks in `Fin n`, and a sequence of switches by the list of positions at which they occur; `Legal` asserts that every switch is permitted.
-- L4DEL: step: This explanation is a condensed rendering of the declaration's own doc comment at the pinned source commit; consult the exact Lean statement below for authority.

