@decl Usa2011P2.key_identity
-- L4DEL: title: The key identity behind the invariance of `invariant`: the weight of a turn at edge `i, i + 1` is `i + (i + 1) = 2 * (i + 3) - 5`
-- L4DEL: intuition: The key identity behind the invariance of `invariant`: the weight of a turn at edge `i, i + 1` is `i + (i + 1) = 2 * (i + 3) - 5`.
-- L4DEL: step: This explanation is a condensed rendering of the declaration's own doc comment at the pinned source commit; consult the exact Lean statement below for authority.

@file Compfiles/Usa2011P2.lean
@decl Usa2011P2.Reachable
-- L4DEL: title: Reachability of configurations
-- L4DEL: intuition: Reachability of configurations. A turn at the edge `i, i + 1` with amount `m` subtracts `m` from the values at the vertices `i` and `i + 1` and adds `2 * m` to the value at the opposite vertex `i + 3` (the unique vertex adjacent to neither of them). The effects of successive turns add up, so a sequence of turns is described by integers `x j`, the sum of the amounts of the turns whose opposite vertex is `j`. Such a turn has edge `j + 2, j + 3`, hence vertex `i` gains `2 * x i` in total and loses `x (i + 2) + x (i + 3)`. Conversely any choice of `x` is realized by doing one turn per edge.
-- L4DEL: step: This explanation is a condensed rendering of the declaration's own doc comment at the pinned source commit; consult the exact Lean statement below for authority.

@file Compfiles/Usa2011P2.lean
@decl Usa2011P2.win_at_zero
-- L4DEL: title: The core existence lemma: a configuration with sum 2011 and vanishing invariant can be won at vertex 0
-- L4DEL: intuition: The core existence lemma: a configuration with sum 2011 and vanishing invariant can be won at vertex 0. With `k` given by `a 1 + 2 * a 2 + 3 * a 3 + 4 * a 4 = 5 * k`, the explicit solution is `x 0 = 0`, `x 1 = -k - a 1`, `x 2 = -2 * k + a 3 + a 4`, `x 3 = -3 * k + a 2 + a 3 + 2 * a 4`, `x 4 = -4 * k + a 2 + 2 * a 3 + 2 * a 4`.
-- L4DEL: step: This explanation is a condensed rendering of the declaration's own doc comment at the pinned source commit; consult the exact Lean statement below for authority.

@file Compfiles/Usa2011P2.lean
@decl Usa2011P2.WinAt
-- L4DEL: title: The game is won at vertex `v` from the configuration `a` if the configuration with value 2011 at `v` and 0 at the other four vertices is reachable from `a`
-- L4DEL: intuition: The game is won at vertex `v` from the configuration `a` if the configuration with value 2011 at `v` and 0 at the other four vertices is reachable from `a`.
-- L4DEL: step: This explanation is a condensed rendering of the declaration's own doc comment at the pinned source commit; consult the exact Lean statement below for authority.

