@decl Usa2012P2.exists_rotation
-- L4DEL: title: Pigeonhole over rotations
-- L4DEL: intuition: Pigeonhole over rotations. Suppose that no rotation in `avoid` moves a point of `S` onto a point of `C`, and that `(432 - #avoid) * k < #S * #C`. Each of the `#S * #C` pairs `(x, c) ∈ S × C` determines a unique rotation sending `x` to `c`, and this rotation lies outside `avoid`; averaging over the `432 - #avoid` allowed rotations, some rotation moves more than `k` points of `S` onto `C`.
-- L4DEL: step: This explanation is a condensed rendering of the declaration's own doc comment at the pinned source commit; consult the exact Lean statement below for authority.

