@file Compfiles/Usa2013P3.lean
@decl Usa2013P3.theta_aux
-- L4DEL: title: The key property of `θ = (e,e,e)`: every token lies on an even number of even-length lines
-- L4DEL: intuition: The key property of `θ = (e,e,e)`: every token lies on an even number of even-length lines. Indeed, with `c = n - 1 - a - b` we have `a + b + c = n - 1`, so among `a % 2`, `b % 2`, `c % 2` the number of values equal to `n % 2` is even.
-- L4DEL: step: This explanation is a condensed rendering of the declaration's own doc comment at the pinned source commit; consult the exact Lean statement below for authority.

@file Compfiles/Usa2013P3.lean
@decl Usa2013P3.Token
-- L4DEL: title: The tokens are indexed by pairs `(a, b)` of natural numbers with `a + b < n`
-- L4DEL: intuition: The tokens are indexed by pairs `(a, b)` of natural numbers with `a + b < n`. One should think of barycentric coordinates `(a, b, c)` with `a + b + c = n - 1`, so that `c = n - 1 - a - b` is determined.
-- L4DEL: step: This explanation is a condensed rendering of the declaration's own doc comment at the pinned source commit; consult the exact Lean statement below for authority.

