@decl Usa2014P4.midphase
-- L4DEL: title: The midgame invariant: with `(0, 0)` and `(5, 0)` occupied, exactly one of `x₀`, `y₀` missing, and the filled neighbor slots `Nx ⊆ xSlots`, `Ny ⊆ ySlots`, `A` can force a win
-- L4DEL: intuition: The midgame invariant: with `(0, 0)` and `(5, 0)` occupied, exactly one of `x₀`, `y₀` missing, and the filled neighbor slots `Nx ⊆ xSlots`, `Ny ⊆ ySlots`, `A` can force a win. `A` replaces the missing distinguished cell and fills one more of its neighbor slots each round; `B` must remove one of the two distinguished cells every round, so eventually one of them is completely surrounded and the endgame lemmas apply.
-- L4DEL: step: This explanation is a condensed rendering of the declaration's own doc comment at the pinned source commit; consult the exact Lean statement below for authority.

