@decl Usa2016P1.not_hasChain_of_le_six
-- L4DEL: title: Any chain on an `n`-element set uses at most `2 ^ n - 1` nonempty subsets, so `n ≤ 6` is impossible since `2 ^ 6 - 1 < 100`
-- L4DEL: intuition: Any chain on an `n`-element set uses at most `2 ^ n - 1` nonempty subsets, so `n ≤ 6` is impossible since `2 ^ 6 - 1 < 100`.
