@file Compfiles/Usa2019P3.lean
@decl Usa2019P3.coeff_stable
-- L4DEL: title: Reduction to monomials: if `f` maps `K` into `K` and its `i`-th coefficient is nonzero, then `f.coeff i * m ^ i ∈ K` for every `m ∈ K`
-- L4DEL: intuition: Reduction to monomials: if `f` maps `K` into `K` and its `i`-th coefficient is nonzero, then `f.coeff i * m ^ i ∈ K` for every `m ∈ K`. The idea: evaluate at `10 ^ E * m` for a huge `E`; the decimal digits of the result are the padded blocks of the digits of `f.coeff i * m ^ i`.
-- L4DEL: step: This explanation is a condensed rendering of the declaration's own doc comment at the pinned source commit; consult the exact Lean statement below for authority.

