@decl Usa2021P2.Park.no_mirror
-- L4DEL: title: The key lemma: a trajectory never contains a turn and its mirror image, i.e
-- L4DEL: intuition: The key lemma: a trajectory never contains a turn and its mirror image, i.e. turns `a → b → c` and `c → b → a` through the same junction. Otherwise the turns adjacent to them at `c` would again be mirror images of each other, with a strictly smaller gap — an infinite descent.
-- L4DEL: step: This explanation is a condensed rendering of the declaration's own doc comment at the pinned source commit; consult the exact Lean statement below for authority.

