@file Compfiles/Usa2022P5.lean
@decl Usa2022P5.not_good_ten
-- L4DEL: title: The lower bound: ten functions do not suffice
-- L4DEL: intuition: The lower bound: ten functions do not suffice. Following the official solution, take `xₙ = -(n + 1)`. For each `n` the support `S(n) = {i | fᵢ(n) ≠ 0}` is nonempty, and there are only `2¹⁰ - 1 = 1023 < 2022` nonempty subsets of a ten-element set, so two supports coincide, contradicting the essentially increasing condition because `x` is strictly decreasing.
-- L4DEL: step: This explanation is a condensed rendering of the declaration's own doc comment at the pinned source commit; consult the exact Lean statement below for authority.

