@decl Usa2022P6.Cover
-- L4DEL: title: Documented declaration: Cover
-- L4DEL: intuition: A *cover* of `G'` relative to the original graph `G`: a finite collection `C` of cliques of `G'` together with a labeling `ℓ` assigning to every edge of `G'` a clique containing its endpoints, such that every clique `K` "owns" at least `3|K|/2 - 2` edges of the original graph `G` (this is the quantity `θ(K)` appearing in `theta_bound`). This is the data maintained by the clique-merging algorithm used in the lower bound proof.
-- L4DEL: step: This explanation is a condensed rendering of the declaration's own doc comment at the pinned source commit; consult the exact Lean statement below for authority.

@file Compfiles/Usa2022P6.lean
@decl Usa2022P6.Cover.merge
-- L4DEL: title: Documented declaration: merge
-- L4DEL: intuition: One merge step of the clique-cover algorithm: if the four edges of some 4-cycle `abcd` in `G'` do not all carry the same label, we may add all missing edges inside the union `V'` of the (two to four) cliques labeling those edges and merge those cliques into a single clique `V'`, obtaining a new valid cover with strictly fewer cliques.
-- L4DEL: step: This explanation is a condensed rendering of the declaration's own doc comment at the pinned source commit; consult the exact Lean statement below for authority.

