@file Compfiles/Usa2025P1.lean
@decl Usa2025P1.residue_mod
-- L4DEL: title: For odd `n` and `1 ≤ ℓ ≤ k`, the residue of `n ^ k` modulo `(2 * n) ^ ℓ` has the form `c * n ^ ℓ` for an odd `c` (so in particular `1 ≤ c`)
-- L4DEL: intuition: For odd `n` and `1 ≤ ℓ ≤ k`, the residue of `n ^ k` modulo `(2 * n) ^ ℓ` has the form `c * n ^ ℓ` for an odd `c` (so in particular `1 ≤ c`). In other words, the `ℓ` rightmost base-`(2 * n)` digits of `n ^ k` are the base-`(2 * n)` digits of `c * n ^ ℓ`.
-- L4DEL: step: This explanation is a condensed rendering of the declaration's own doc comment at the pinned source commit; consult the exact Lean statement below for authority.

