@file Compfiles/Usa2025P2.lean
@decl Usa2025P2.core_pigeonhole
-- L4DEL: title: The combinatorial heart of the problem
-- L4DEL: intuition: The combinatorial heart of the problem. Let `s` be a set of `k + 1` real numbers (with `k ≥ 1`). Then it is impossible that for every `i ∈ s`, the polynomial `∏_{r ∈ s \ {i}} (X - r)` has a zero coefficient among the positions `1, ..., k - 1`. Indeed, two such polynomials would share the position `t` of a zero coefficient (pigeonhole), forcing the common sub-product `∏_{r ∈ s \ {i₁, i₂}} (X - r)` to have two consecutive zero coefficients, contradicting Rolle's theorem.
-- L4DEL: step: This explanation is a condensed rendering of the declaration's own doc comment at the pinned source commit; consult the exact Lean statement below for authority.

@file Compfiles/Usa2025P2.lean
@decl Usa2025P2.dvd_X_pow_two_iterate_derivative
-- L4DEL: title: If the coefficients of `x^(t-1)` and `x^t` of `R` both vanish, then `X^2` divides the `(t-1)`-st derivative of `R`
-- L4DEL: intuition: If the coefficients of `x^(t-1)` and `x^t` of `R` both vanish, then `X^2` divides the `(t-1)`-st derivative of `R`.
-- L4DEL: step: This explanation is a condensed rendering of the declaration's own doc comment at the pinned source commit; consult the exact Lean statement below for authority.

